# Firmware update over USB DFU {#dfu-update}
Hold BOOT0 high and press RESET to enter the ROM DFU bootloader. The board enumerates as "STM32 BOOTLOADER" (0483:df11). Flash the signed image with dfu-util -a 0 -s 0x08000000:leave -D gw-fw.bin. The :leave suffix restarts the board into the new firmware when flashing is done.

## Over-the-air updates (A/B slots) {#ota-ab}
OTA downloads the new image into the inactive slot while the gateway keeps running. After the SHA-256 and ECDSA signature check passes, the bootloader swaps slots on the next reboot. If the new firmware does not confirm itself within 3 boots, the bootloader rolls back to the previous slot.

## Boot loop recovery {#boot-loop}
When the status LED blinks red three times and the board resets every few seconds, the application is crashing before it confirms the slot. Wait for the automatic rollback after 3 attempts, or hold the USER button for 10 s during power-up to force the factory image.

## Watchdog timeout {#watchdog}
The independent watchdog (IWDG) is started by the bootloader with a 4 s timeout and cannot be stopped. The main loop must refresh it; a task blocked on a mutex or a long flash erase without refresh causes a watchdog reset, logged as RST_CAUSE=IWDG after reboot.

## Serial console settings {#uart-console}
The debug console is on USART2 (pins PA2/PA3) at 115200 baud, 8N1, no flow control. Log lines start with a millisecond timestamp. Use the command `log level debug` to raise the verbosity until the next reboot.

## Sleep modes and power consumption {#power}
In Stop 2 mode with the radio off the board draws 4.2 uA from the battery; with LoRa receive windows every 60 s the average is 38 uA. A 2400 mAh cell lasts about 5 years at that rate. USB power keeps the MCU in Run mode.

## LED codes {#led-codes}
Green steady: connected. Green blinking: joining the network. Amber: firmware update in progress, do not remove power. Red, three blinks then reset: boot failure (see boot loop recovery). Red steady: hardware fault, check the log.

## Factory reset {#factory-reset}
Hold the USER button for 10 s while the gateway is running. Configuration, Wi-Fi credentials and certificates are erased; the firmware image is kept. The LED blinks amber while the configuration partition is erased.

## Wi-Fi provisioning {#wifi-provisioning}
On first boot, or after a factory reset, the gateway opens a BLE provisioning service for 5 minutes. Use the mobile app to send the SSID and passphrase. WPA3-Personal and WPA2-Personal are supported; enterprise (802.1X) networks are not.

## Certificate rotation {#cert-rotation}
Device certificates expire after 397 days. The gateway requests a new certificate 30 days before expiry over the provisioning API and stores it in the secure element (ATECC608B). Rotation fails if the clock is wrong; check NTP first.

## CAN bus termination {#can-termination}
Both ends of the CAN bus need a 120 ohm terminator. Set DIP switch 2 to ON on the gateway if it is at the end of the bus. Measure between CAN_H and CAN_L with power off: 60 ohm means both terminators are present.

## Log levels and remote logs {#logging}
Levels are error, warn, info and debug. Remote logging sends warn and above to the syslog server configured in the cloud console. Debug logs are only kept in RAM and are lost on reboot.

## Cihazın sıfırlanması ve güncelleme {#tr-guncelleme}
Cihaz sürekli yeniden başlıyorsa uygulama yazılımı çöküyor olabilir. Üç denemeden sonra önyükleyici eski yazılıma otomatik olarak geri döner. Güncelleme sırasında kehribar ışık yanarken cihazın gücünü kesmeyin.

## Pil ömrü {#tr-pil}
Pil ömrü radyo kullanımına bağlıdır. Uyku modunda cihaz 4,2 uA çeker; her dakika dinleme penceresi açılırsa ortalama akım 38 uA olur ve 2400 mAh pil yaklaşık beş yıl dayanır.

